# The spy checks are started within a millisecond or two of the result
# they look at. Which of the two comes first differs from call to call.
watch spy1 looks at another object as it changes

# At second 22 the host's check and a check of a service on it come due
# within a few milliseconds of each other. A service result adds the
# host's state to the host's flap history, so which result is read first
# decides what the spy sees from then on. The reference read the service
# first. In real time the order is not the same from run to run; the play
# on the simulated clock keeps the reference's order and compares the spy.
ignore-real spy1 the order of two results a few milliseconds apart
# The same order decides when the service's notification is tried.
ignore-log-real a;s the order of two results a few milliseconds apart
